This is a fork of the Ramses code on my Bitbucket account,
obtained on 12/May/2020 via:

$> git clone https://tepper@bitbucket.org/tepper/ramses.git


It is the (ideally) latest version of Ramses available
through Bitbucket:

$> git clone https://bitbucket.org/rteyssie/ramses

I try my best to keep the latter up-to-date via:

$> git remote update; git status

And in case of new commits:

$> git pull

NOTE: This copy contains my own changes in patch/tepper,
which are however not sent for pull requests from the main repo.
After each update of the main branch I update my fork using
FileMerge to compare and update my patched files.

***************************************************
ABOUT UPDATING IN LINE WITH THE MAIN RAMSES REPO
***************************************************

The current strategy to achieve a seamless integration of changes to the new repo into my patches is the following:
1. git pull the main ramses code (~/codes/ramses/)
2. from the list of file changes, find file matches in patch/tepper via:
	$> find . filename
3. diff relevant files (see 2. above) between main ramses code and *UNCHANGED* main ramses_fork (~/codes/ramses_fork/)
4. synchronyse ramses_fork via Bitbucket
5. git pull ramses_fork
6. Using FileMerge, copy the new changes of the relevant files (see 2. above) into their corresponding copy in patch/tepper/
